**How to implement.** S6 prerequisite/closure for 001 §H and §S6: the shared item contracts MUST land here so experiment copying includes item mapping before S7. The item model becomes a library kind with its file, its schema and its import, and the built-in item models ship in the Built-in catalogue (001 §A 'Library extensions: … .item-model-json'; 001 §B; 001 §I; the S7.1 brief: LibraryEntryKind gains it, `.item-model-json` with a schema, CatalogueImport gains saveItemModel, the built-in item models are written once through the export path and added to Catalogue/Builtin/ with the manifest updated, and there is no code seed; .spec-md §3.14; step 24: 'S7.1 adds the item-model kind'; step 57: a section that adds a built-in kind changes the integrity counts in the step that adds it). The kind, its rows and the facts that count them land together, because `BuiltInCatalogueIntegrityTests` requires every kind of `LibraryEntryKind.all` to have rows. (1) `OpticalConstructor.Domain/LibraryEntryFiles.fs` (steps 24, 25, 137) opens `ItemModels`; each doc is one to three lines citing spec 0050 S7.1. (a) `LibraryEntryKind` gains `ItemModelEntryKind` after `CategoryEntryKind`: `value` 7 (`tryOfWire 7` answers it), extension `.item-model-json` (001 §A), schema version 1; `all` lists the seven in tag order, and its doc and step 24's 'S7.1 adds' remark say so. (b) Beside step 24's id extensions, `type ItemModelId with member this.toLibraryEntryId : LibraryEntryId`, the same GUID; after `EntryReference` (step 137), `type ItemModelVersionId with member this.entryReference : EntryReference`, the `EntryVersionReference` of that GUID at that version. No conversion goes the other way (ELEV006). (c) `LibraryEntryPayload` gains `ItemModelPayload of ItemModelForm`, of kind `ItemModelEntryKind`. (d) The builder `static member ofItemModel (version : VersionNumber) (provenance : EntryProvenance) (entry : ItemModelEntry) : Result<LibraryEntryContent, LibraryEntryError>`, as step 25's preset builders: an `entry.protection` other than `provenance.protection` is `ProvenanceMismatchErr` naming the entry; otherwise the content holds the entry's id, name, `categoryOpt = None`, `descriptionOpt = Some entry.description` and `ItemModelPayload entry.model`. The decoder `member this.toItemModel : Result<ItemModelEntry, LibraryEntryError>` is marked as step 25's decoders are (`StorageBoundary`: the file's entry GUID becomes the item model's id): another payload is `EntryKindMismatchErr`, no description `MissingEntryFieldErr`, and the protection comes from the provenance. (e) `references` (step 137): an item model answers `[]`, because its components are inline forms, not entries. (2) Every match on `LibraryEntryKind` or `LibraryEntryPayload` the compiler now reports incomplete (FS0025 is an error) gains the case, and no wildcard is added. Among them: `OpticalConstructor.Domain/CatalogueImport.fs`' apply order (step 94: item models after detectors); `OpticalConstructor.Storage/SchemaValidation.fs`' `schemaFile` and its per-kind lazies (step 30: `schema/library-item-model.schema.json`); `OpticalConstructor.Storage/LibraryDatabaseStore.fs`' `facetRows` (step 64: an item model has none); and `OpticalConstructor.Ui/ConstructorUiIdOfDomain.fs`' `LibraryEntryKind.caption` (step 107: `Item model`). (3) The import seam: the brief's 'CatalogueImport gains saveItemModel' is realised on step 94's kind-neutral seam. `InMemoryCatalogueStores` gains `itemModels : ItemModelProxy`, built by `CatalogueImportProxy.createInMemory ()` with `ItemModelProxy.createInMemory ()` (step 209). A put of an item-model id its map does not hold decodes the envelope with `toItemModel` and pushes `{ version = content.version; entry = … }` through `saveItemModel`, as step 94's adapters push the other kinds; `UndecodableEntryErr`, or an `ItemModelError` answered as `ImportRejectedErr` with its `describe`, stops the put before the map changes. The database seam (`createInDatabase`, step 95) already stores every kind's envelope and is unchanged. (4) New `OpticalConstructor.Storage/schema/library-item-model.schema.json`, written as step 30's per-kind schemas (`$id` `https://berreman/schema/library-item-model.json`, referencing `library-common.schema.json`): `schema` is `{ kind: 7, version: <a positive integer> }` unconditionally; under `schema.version` 1 every key is present and no other, `id` a GUID, `name` a non-empty string, `categoryOpt` `null`, `descriptionOpt` a string, `payload` the item-model case with its form bound by the serializer, `provenance` one of the common shapes and `contentHash` the hash pattern. It is a `Content` item copied `PreserveNewest` beside the other library schemas in `OpticalConstructor.Storage.fsproj`, with no comment. (5) The built-ins go through the export path once, as step 35's did. New throw-away `Berreman/OpticalConstructor/Catalogue/export-item-models.fsx` loads the Release x64 build exactly as step 35's tool did (`#I` the `OpticalConstructor.Tests` output, `#r` the Domain and Storage assemblies and what they load, no `#r "nuget:"`). It reads the catalogue through `(CatalogueProxy.create (FolderName (Path.Combine(__SOURCE_DIRECTORY__, "Builtin")))).readCatalogue ()` (step 33), seals the eleven item models below as `ProtectedBuiltIn` entries at `VersionNumber.first` under `BuiltInProvenance CatalogueIds.builtInCatalogue` through `ofItemModel` and `sealed` (step 30), builds `CatalogueData.tryCreate CatalogueIds.builtInCatalogue (CatalogueName "Built-in") VersionNumber.first` over the catalogue's envelopes followed by the eleven, and writes it back through the same proxy's `writeCatalogue`. Any `Error` prints its case and exits 1. Build, run `dotnet fsi Berreman/OpticalConstructor/Catalogue/export-item-models.fsx` once from the repository root, and commit the eleven new files and the rewritten `.catalogue-json`; every other entry file is rewritten byte for byte, so git shows no change in it. The catalogue keeps version 1, because no release exists; its manifest hash changes, which is what the start-up import compares (001 §B). The eleven, by `ItemModelIds` member, name, form and description: (a) `realLinearPolarizerModelId`, `Real linear polarizer`, `OpticalElementModel (RealPolarizerModel ExtinctionRatioLeakage)`, described 'A linear polarizer with an extinction ratio and an axis offset; at its defaults it is the ideal linear polarizer.'; (b) `retarderPlateModelId`, `Retarder plate`, `OpticalElementModel (RetarderPlateModel ConstantRetardance)`, described 'A wave plate with a retardance and a fast-axis offset; at its defaults it is a quarter-wave plate.'; (c) `circularPolarizerModelId`, `Circular polarizer (linear polarizer and retarder)`, `OpticalElementModel (CompoundModel [ { form = RealPolarizerModel ExtinctionRatioLeakage; offset = 0° }; { form = RetarderPlateModel ConstantRetardance; offset = 45° } ])`, described 'A linear polarizer followed in light order by a retarder whose fast axis sits at 45° plus its own offset.'; (d) `blackBoxMuellerModelId`, `Black-box Mueller matrix`, `OpticalElementModel (BlackBoxMuellerModel SixteenElementMueller)`, described 'A sample known only by its sixteen Mueller elements at reference orientation; at its defaults it is the identity.'; (e) `emptySlotModelId`, `Empty slot (air)`, `EmptySlotModel`, described 'Nothing in the beam: the identity, the calibration reference.'; (f) `intensityDetectorModelId`, `Intensity detector (gain, dark offset and noise)`, `IntensityDetectorModel detectorNoiseAxes`, described 'Records the intensity S0 through a gain and a dark offset, with the decent-lab noise budget.'; (g) `muellerPolarimeterModelId`, `Mueller polarimeter`, `MuellerPolarimeterModel detectorNoiseAxes`, described 'Records a full Mueller matrix, with the decent-lab noise budget.'; (h) `ellipsometerModelId`, `Ellipsometer (noise budget)`, `EllipsometerModel detectorNoiseAxes`, described 'Records Psi and Delta, with the decent-lab noise budget.'. Their files are named by step 24's rule (`Real linear polarizer.item-model-json` and the rest, exactly this step's effects), LF-only, and `git check-ignore` reports none of them. Step 212 deletes the tool. (6) `OpticalConstructor.Tests/BuiltinCatalogue.fs` (step 41, linked into the UI suite) gains `itemModels () : ItemModelVersion list`, the catalogue's item-model rows decoded in row order at their versions, and `itemModel (id : ItemModelId) : ItemModelVersion`, failing with the id when the catalogue holds none, each with a one-line doc. (7) Tests. `BuiltInCatalogueIntegrityTests`' `the shipped Built-in catalogue is whole: every file validates, every hash matches its manifest row, ids are unique and every built-in kind is present` (step 57) counts 11 item models beside its other kinds. It gains `the shipped item models include every required form under their well-known ids`: `BuiltinCatalogue.itemModels ()` holds exactly the eleven above by id, name and form, each at version 1 and `ProtectedBuiltIn`, and each envelope's provenance is `BuiltInProvenance CatalogueIds.builtInCatalogue`. `LibraryEntryFilesTests`' `every library entry kind round-trips its wire tag and renders its 001 extension` (step 24) covers seven tags, `None` for 0 and 8, and `.item-model-json`. It gains `an item-model builder and decoder are inverse, and a protection its provenance disagrees with is refused`: a test-local `UserManaged` compound under `UserProvenance` decodes to itself through `ofItemModel` and `toItemModel`; a `ProtectedBuiltIn` entry under `UserProvenance` answers `ProvenanceMismatchErr`; and `toItemModel` of Silicon's content answers `EntryKindMismatchErr`. `CatalogueImportProxyTests`' `importCatalogue pushes every entry once, categories then materials then samples then presets, through the exact signatures` expects the tape to end with every item-model envelope, in row order, after the detectors. The same one-time exporter MUST also write Light source (preset binding).item-model-json under ItemModelIds.sourcePresetItemModelId, form SourcePresetItemModel, version 1 and ProtectedBuiltIn, with a description identifying the typed physics binding it reuses. Its manifest row and hash MUST be produced by the same export path. The same one-time exporter MUST also write Ideal polarizer (preset binding).item-model-json under ItemModelIds.idealPolarizerItemModelId, form IdealPolarizerItemModel, version 1 and ProtectedBuiltIn, with a description identifying the typed physics binding it reuses. Its manifest row and hash MUST be produced by the same export path. The same one-time exporter MUST also write Sample by stack.item-model-json under ItemModelIds.stackSampleItemModelId, form StackSampleItemModel, version 1 and ProtectedBuiltIn, with a description identifying the typed physics binding it reuses. Its manifest row and hash MUST be produced by the same export path. The import-tape fixture MUST first obtain all decisions, assert no writes, and then explicitly apply their defaults as step 94 requires before asserting the expanded item-model tape. In the throw-away export-item-models.fsx ONLY, detectorNoiseAxes MUST be derived from BerremanTests.NoiseParam.decentLab in the built BerremanTests assembly, reading its three values once and passing elevated ParameterValues to ItemParameterAxis.detectorNoiseAxes. The script MAY reference that test assembly; no product project may do so. It MUST NOT transcribe the bench constants. The persisted catalogue contains the generated axes. Step 212 deletes the exporter, and step 339's parity fact compares the promoted budget with these catalogue defaults. EntryFileJson.fs MUST encode ParameterKind in the detector axis list through its integer value and decode through tryOfWire. An unrecognized tag MUST become the typed file-read error at this serialization boundary, never an unrecognized Domain case or an exception. It MUST use the canonical JSON stack already used for ItemModel payloads.

**Acceptance.** After the kind lands, `LibraryEntryKind.all` MUST list seven kinds with `ItemModelEntryKind` at tag 7 and `.item-model-json`, an item-model entry MUST seal, write and read back through `library-item-model.schema.json`, the in-memory import MUST push item models through `ItemModelProxy.saveItemModel`, and `Berreman/OpticalConstructor/Catalogue/Builtin/` MUST hold the eleven built-in item models listed in its manifest, none git-ignored; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `the shipped Built-in catalogue is whole: every file validates, every hash matches its manifest row, ids are unique and every built-in kind is present`, `the shipped item models include every required form under their well-known ids`, `every library entry kind round-trips its wire tag and renders its 001 extension`, `an item-model builder and decoder are inverse, and a protection its provenance disagrees with is refused` and `importCatalogue pushes every entry once, categories then materials then samples then presets, through the exact signatures`, the count rising by 2; ui-smoke MUST pass with its count unchanged; ui-tests MUST pass over the selected classes, their count unchanged; and build, elevation and the fourteen s22 invariants MUST pass.
